# datalab — Cursor rules

Full project context — architecture, codebase layout, pipeline authoring
rules, build/test/deploy commands, common tasks, gotchas, and security — lives
in [AGENTS.md](../../AGENTS.md). Read it before editing.

Quick pointers:

- **Pipelines are config-driven**: a target table is ONE YAML artifact
  (`config/<catalog>/<schema>/<table>.yml`; in this repo the example lives at
  `examples/customer_sales/config/customer_sales/`) — author it with the
  `author-ldp-artifact` skill; full reference + SDP capability matrix in
  docs/FRAMEWORK.md. Folder paths mirror the UC namespace (docs/NAMING.md).
  Never hand-write `dp.*` wiring unless the matrix says the framework can't
  express it (`author-sdp-pipeline` skill).
- When SDP code IS written: **`from pyspark import pipelines as dp`** — never
  `import dlt` (deprecated). Dataset functions return DataFrames; no
  `.write`, `.saveAsTable`, `.start()`, or `.collect()` inside them. Upserts
  use AUTO CDC (`target.cdc` in the artifact); data quality uses
  **databrickslabs/dqx** via the framework — `dp.expect_*` is retired here.
- `src/` holds ONLY the framework (`src/datalab/`). Domain business logic
  lives in the domain package (`src/<catalog>_etl/transforms/`, in this repo
  under `examples/customer_sales/`) as pure, unit-tested `@transform` functions.
  Parameters come from the pipeline `configuration` mapping via
  `datalab.config.pipeline_conf` — never hardcode catalogs/schemas/paths.
- Deploy = **Declarative Automation Bundle**: `databricks.yml` +
  `examples/*/resources/*.yml` (adopters: `resources/*.yml`), targets `dev`
  (mode: development) / `stage` / `prod`. `make validate` before pushing
  bundle changes.
- **MANDATORY branch-first protocol**: before editing ANY file, verify a
  work branch is checked out — if on `main`, your FIRST action is
  `git switch main && git pull && git switch -c <feature|fix|debug>/<slug>`.
  Never edit, commit, or push while on `main`; one PR per branch; head
  branches are auto-deleted on merge (AGENTS.md "Branching & releases").
  Enforced by `.cursor/hooks/branch_guard.py` (file edits + git
  commit/push-to-main are denied on `main`) and `.githooks/pre-commit`.
- Dependencies are **uv-only**: `pyproject.toml` + committed `uv.lock`
  (`make lock` after edits; CI runs `uv sync --frozen`). Never add
  databricks-connect to this venv — it conflicts with the pyspark dev dep.
- CI (`.github/workflows/common-ci-steps.yml`) runs ruff + validate-configs +
  pytest (local Spark) + `bundle validate`; CD deploys via **GitHub OIDC**
  (no client secret). The OIDC subject must match
  `repo:<owner>/<repo>:environment:<target>`. See docs/CICD.md.
- Production-sensitive files are protected by
  `.claude/hooks/protected_files_guard.py` and `.githooks/pre-commit`. Keep
  both + the AGENTS.md "Protected file surface" table in sync when you change
  the set.
- **One PR format for everything.** All PRs use
  `.github/pull_request_template.md`. When opening a PR from the CLI, fill
  that template into a body file and run `gh pr create --body-file <file>`
  (or `--web`). A `beforeShellExecution` hook
  (`.cursor/hooks/pr_template_guard.py`) blocks `gh pr create` that bypasses
  the template; CI re-checks every PR body.
